{"content":[{"c":["SETH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Third son of Adam and Eve, replacing Abel, whom Cain murdered (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.4.25","r":"Gen.4.25","rawR":"Gen.4.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.4.25","value":"Gen.4.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 4:25"},"). He appears as the firstborn son of Adam in the genealogies of ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.5.3-8","r":"Gen.5.3-8","rawR":"Gen.5.3-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.5.3-8","value":"Gen.5.3-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Genesis 5:3-8"},", ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.1.1","r":"1Chr.1.1","rawR":"1Chr.1.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.1.1","value":"1Chr.1.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 1:1"}," (",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," “Sheth”), and ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.3.38","r":"Luke.3.38","rawR":"Luke.3.38","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.3.38","value":"Luke.3.38"}],"t":"ref","v":"Luke 3:38"},". It was through Seth’s line that Jesus was born. Seth was the father of Enosh and lived 912 years."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Genealogy of Jesus Christ"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Seth","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 4:25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.4.25","rawQueryValue":"Gen.4.25","sourceRefExact":"Gen.4.25"},{"anchorText":"Genesis 5:3-8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.5.3-8","rawQueryValue":"Gen.5.3-8","sourceRefExact":"Gen.5.3-8"},{"anchorText":"1 Chronicles 1:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.1.1","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.